          "court": "Supreme Court of Hawai'i",
          "year": 1996,
          "date_decided": "1996-12-16",
          "holding": "The court held that the family court may exercise chapter 587 protective powers whenever it has the necessary information, regardless of whether the case began under chapter 571 or on a formal chapter 587 petition, but reversed the portion of the order requiring DHS foster board payments after the minor turned eighteen.",
